infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title LAST_VALUE — default frame vs the fix
  desc With an ORDER BY the name promises the last row, but the frame decides reality
  compares
    - label Default frame (the trap)
      children
        - label Frame ends at CURRENT ROW
          desc ORDER BY silently adds RANGE UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW
        - label Returns the current row value
          desc The last row of the frame is the current row, not the partition end
        - label Wrong on every row but the last
          desc The biggest-deal-so-far column shows the wrong number everywhere
    - label Extended frame (the fix)
      children
        - label ROWS UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING
          desc One added clause stretches the frame to the partition end
        - label Returns the partition last row
          desc The true final value by the ORDER BY
        - label Correct on every row
          desc FIRST_VALUE looks right by accident; LAST_VALUE needs this fix
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
